<title>MEXICO: Mexico expects to double coffee exports to Europe.</title>
<headline>Mexico expects to double coffee exports to Europe.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico should more than double its coffee exports to the European Union in 1997 to about 500,000 60-kg bags from 240,000 bags in 1996, a coffee executive said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The removal of a four percent tariff on Mexican coffee exports to Europe as of January 1 is encouraging greater exports, vice-president of  Agroindustrias Unidas de Mexico Pedro Tabares said. Tabares spoke at a two-day Mexico-European Union Agribusiness Forum.</p>
<p>The company's coffee arm, Omnicafe, currently has between 15 and 16 percent of Mexico's total coffee export market share, Tabares said.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
